</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 480)</h2>
<p><b>Optimized media now looks like the original on any OCIO config.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: optimized stand-ins played back washed out</b> on the ACES config built into Asobi. The stand-in is encoded through a log curve and the sidecar records that curve by name — but Asobi decided whether it could decode that name by looking it up in the config's list of color-space names. That list omits aliases: the built-in config calls the space <code>ACEScct</code> and accepts <code>ACES - ACEScct</code> only as an alias, so the name every sidecar records read as missing, playback quietly fell back to scene-linear, and a log picture shown as linear is milky and flat. Asobi now asks the config to resolve the name instead of searching a list, which works whichever name the config prefers. <b>Existing stand-ins are fine and do not need re-rendering</b> — the encode was always correct; only playback misread it.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: zooming past 1:1 switched to the original frame but kept decoding it as the stand-in's log curve</b>, so every zoom looked crushed and blue. The original is decoded as itself now, and the color chip follows.</li>
<li><b>The color chip shows what is actually decoding.</b> While a stand-in is on screen it reads the stand-in's space rather than the original's, and the Color pipeline popover says so — the Input picker is labeled "Input · original" and describes the space exports use. Previously the chip advertised a space the renderer wasn't using, which made a wrong picture look correct.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: "Delete Optimized Media" for the current shot reported nothing to delete</b> while the OPTIMIZED badge was showing. It was looking up the stand-in's own filename rather than the shot's, and asking for <code>&lt;name&gt;.mov.mov</code>. Deleting now also brings the original back on screen straight away instead of at the next clip change. The same mistake made "Optimize This Shot" a silent no-op on a shot already playing a stand-in.</li>
<li><b>Optimizing now fails loudly instead of quietly.</b> If the active config can't build the requested log conversion, Asobi says which spaces and stops, rather than writing a stand-in with no transform baked in whose sidecar claims otherwise.</li>
<li>The badge reads OPTIMIZED, and the Color pipeline panel is spelled US English.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
